    "title": "PhotoSwipe image galleries",
    "subtitle": "Open, zoom and explore images",
    "excerpt": "PhotoSwipe support is available in the development version after v2.1.0.Add photoswipe=true to a masonry or carousel include. No page YAML setting isneeded. Each gallery opens its own sequence; images remain ordinary links whenJavaScript is disabled or the library cannot load.",
    "content": "PhotoSwipe support is available in the development version after v2.1.0. Add photoswipe=true to a masonry or carousel include. No page YAML setting is needed. Each gallery opens its own sequence; images remain ordinary links when JavaScript is disabled or the library cannot load.   Masonry gallery   Click an image, or focus its link and press Enter. Inside the viewer, use the arrow keys to change images and Escape to close it. Focus returns to the image you opened. On touchscreens, swipe between images and pinch to zoom.                                                     {% include_cached snippets/masonry.html internal=\"gallery\" index_items=6 photoswipe=true %}   Carousel gallery   The carousel uses a separate group. Its slide remains in place while the viewer is open. PhotoSwipe loads only when you open an image, respects reduced motion and discovers image dimensions without a Jekyll image-processing plugin.          \t   \t   \t   \t   \t   \t  \t     Ⅱ                   \t  \t                \t  \t                \t  \t                Previous                Next      {% include_cached snippets/carousel.html internal=\"gallery\" index_items=3 interval=0 controls=true indicators=true photoswipe=true %}   The examples use the existing image_col: gallery static-file defaults. External image lists work too. See gallery setup and PhotoSwipe requirements.",
